From: pat <pi3iman@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] lib: wire up CONFIG_UMASH

Kconfig/Makefile plumbing for lib/umash.c: a bool gated to ARM64,
since the PMULL fast path has no software fallback. No special
CFLAGS are needed for lib/umash.o -- see 999-umash-01's commit
message for why its PMULL inline asm works fine under the kernel's
default -mgeneral-regs-only.

Unlike CONFIG_XXHASH (a promptless `bool`/`tristate` with no prompt
string, only ever turned on via `select` from another symbol),
CONFIG_UMASH gets an actual prompt. A promptless symbol can only be
enabled via `select`; Kconfig's syncconfig silently drops a raw
CONFIG_FOO=y line for one when merging a config fragment, since there
is no user-facing choice to record a value against. Confirmed this
the hard way: a first real build had CONFIG_UMASH=y sitting correctly
in the merged .config.set/.config.target, and it still vanished from
the final .config, so lib/umash.o never got built. Nothing in this
series selects UMASH from elsewhere, so it needs the prompt to be
directly settable from the mt7622 subtarget config-6.12 the way the
line was always intended to work.

Signed-off-by: pat <pi3iman@gmail.com>
---
--- a/lib/Kconfig
+++ b/lib/Kconfig
@@ -279,6 +279,10 @@ config CRC8
 config XXHASH
 	tristate

+config UMASH
+	bool "UMASH hash function (arm64/PMULL)"
+	depends on ARM64
+
 config AUDIT_GENERIC
 	bool
 	depends on AUDIT && !AUDIT_ARCH
--- a/lib/Makefile
+++ b/lib/Makefile
@@ -165,6 +165,7 @@ obj-$(CONFIG_CRC4)	+= crc4.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_CRC7)	+= crc7.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_LIBCRC32C)	+= libcrc32c.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_CRC8)	+= crc8.o
+obj-$(CONFIG_UMASH)	+= umash.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_CRC64_ROCKSOFT) += crc64-rocksoft.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_XXHASH)	+= xxhash.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_GENERIC_ALLOCATOR) += genalloc.o
